A||||3||Frank R||Solving mechanical problems  a mystery||||6||
Z||000000||Frank R||04-28-2000||07:39 PM||||The ability to solve a car's problems is like a mystery.  You must extract enough info to make a rational decision.  A seasoned mechanic can often make better decisions because the symptoms have been observed before.  With any difficulty, make some notes about what is happening and how it might be different than before.  In many cases after gathering all the info, a clear cut decision cannot be made as to the repair required.  This very true with electronics.  Many systems work with an`other part and all the pieces/parts must be repaired or checked.   As an example.  Clutch systems work with many parts as the clutch and pressure plate are considered as a unit, the throw out bearing, the bearing fork, the slave cylinder, the master cylinder and lastly the hydraulics[read brake fluid].  The greater the amount of info, the better the chance of correct repair.  Some times this info can actually lead to an overall improvement or design change.......Frank R...||||reg||6
Z||000001||Gokart||04-29-2000||04:59 AM||||Sounds like good advice and you know your stuff Frank! Glad your here! I'm a carpenters son that didn't know the difference between a cap or rotor a few years back <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"> This forum as helped save me time and money over and over again. Thanks to you and others, guys like me are slowing becoming their own mechanics! I love working on my car and if I could do things over again I'd gone to a tech/trade school and I'd be "twisting wrenches" for a living!||||reg||14
Z||000002||mwbackus||04-29-2000||07:11 AM||||Sounds like good advice to me.  I could only add that folks include a short description of the vehicle in question when submitting a problem to the forum.  The "interests" section of ones user profile is an excellent area to describe your Fiero.<P>Mike B.||||reg||14
Z||000003||DXR_DAD||04-29-2000||02:03 PM||||Good info Frank, This fourm has given me alot of need info on the Fiero. I have read many stories about people buying a Fiero that the owner was feed up with all the repairs and repair bills, but they did not get informed! or even try to get the info the needed, thus they sell the car for 0.00 or close to it.<BR>One story in mind on the clutch thing.<BR>The seller said his mechanic told him the car needed a clutch $1,000-$1,500 to repair<BR>so he sold the car for $800 it was a 85GT I think. The new owner found the info on bent clutch pedals, he replaced it for $10.00. The runs great! the clutch was fine.<P>This has to be the best fourm on the web!!<BR>and I'm glad to be a part of it.||||reg||1
